  "Number": 29,
  "Question": "A particle projected vertically upward reaches, at the end of \\(t\\) seconds, an elevation of \\(s\\) feet where \\(s=160t-16t^2.\\) The highest elevation is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(800\\)",
    "B": "\\(640\\)",
    "C": "\\(400\\)",
    "D": "\\(320\\)",
    "E": "\\(160\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "To find the greatest height, rewrite the formula as a constant minus a nonnegative square:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\ns&=160t-16t^2\\\\\n&=-16(t^2-10t)\\\\\n&=-16\\bigl((t-5)^2-25\\bigr)\\\\\n&=400-16(t-5)^2.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nSince \\((t-5)^2\\ge0\\), the elevation cannot exceed \\(400\\) feet. Equality occurs at \\(t=5\\) seconds, which is an allowed time after launch. Therefore the highest elevation is \\(\\boxed{400\\text{ feet}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
